  "Question": "Two lines intersect. One angle is \\(40^\\circ\\) greater than its adjacent supplementary angle. What is the measure of this angle in degrees?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "110",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let this angle be \\(x^\\circ\\). Then \\(x-(180-x)=40\\), \\(2x=220\\), and \\(x=110\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Remove the excess\n\nThe adjacent supplementary angles total \\(180^\\circ\\). Subtracting the larger angle's \\(40^\\circ\\) excess leaves two equal amounts, so the smaller angle is\n\\[\n\\frac{180^\\circ-40^\\circ}{2}=70^\\circ.\n\\]\nThe requested larger angle is therefore \\(70^\\circ+40^\\circ=110^\\circ\\).",
